0.550 0.650 0.780 RG 1.10 w 54.0 715.0 m 558.0 715.0 l S
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 693.0 Td (There are three layers, and they are kept strictly separate. Understanding the split explains most design decisions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 679.2 Td (in the code.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.5 Tf 0.100 0.280 0.480 rg 54.0 653.9 Td (Layer 1 - Description \(what the robot IS\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 637.1 Td (A set of xacro files that declare the robot: link geometry, joints, sensors, the hardware interfaces ros2_control will) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 623.6 Td (drive, and the Gazebo plugins. Nothing here knows about the mission. Every dimension is a named constant,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 610.1 Td (declared once.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.5 Tf 0.100 0.280 0.480 rg 54.0 584.8 Td (Layer 2 - Simulation assets \(where the robot LIVES\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 568.0 Td (World files \(room, walls, shelf, objects at their starting poses\), object models, and one launch file that starts every) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 554.5 Td (process in a deterministic order. Nothing here knows about kinematics.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.5 Tf 0.100 0.280 0.480 rg 54.0 529.3 Td (Layer 3 - Behaviour \(what the robot DOES\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 512.5 Td (Pure-Python kinematics and choreography with no ROS imports at all, plus two ROS nodes: one that turns camera) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 499.0 Td (frames into detections, and one state machine that runs the mission. Because the kinematics and choreography are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.130 0.130 0.130 rg 54.0 485.4 Td (ROS-free, the entire motion plan can be validated by a unit test on any machine without launching Gazebo.) Tj ET
0.990 0.960 0.900 rg 54.0 410.1 504.0 66.6 re f
0.850 0.620 0.150 rg 54.0 410.1 3.5 66.6 re f
BT /F2 10.0 Tf 0.080 0.200 0.400 rg 66.0 459.7 Td (The most important consequence of this split) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.160 0.160 0.180 rg 66.0 446.2 Td (Geometry is declared in the xacro files and mirrored as constants in ik.py. A test asserts that every motion the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.160 0.160 0.180 rg 66.0 433.0 Td (mission can command is reachable within the declared joint limits. If you change a link length in the xacro, you must) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.4 Tf 0.160 0.160 0.180 rg 66.0 419.9 Td (change it in ik.py too - and the test is what will catch you if you forget.) Tj ET
